def H(code, d, q, right, wrong, e): return B.hand(code, d, q, right, wrong, e)

H("677.d.1.A",3,"Which event would most clearly create a need for digital forensics?","a company discovers an employee copied confidential files to a personal drive",["a monitor is replaced","a keyboard is cleaned","a desk is moved"],"Suspected data theft calls for an investigation.")
H("677.d.1.A",4,"Digital forensics helps an organization determine:","what happened, how it happened, and who was involved",["which paint color to buy","how to schedule lunch breaks","what font to use in reports"],"Forensics answers questions about incidents.")
H("677.d.1.B",3,"Which credential is aimed at digital forensics professionals?","GIAC Certified Forensic Examiner (GCFE)",["Certified Public Accountant","Commercial Pilot License","Food Safety Manager"],"GCFE validates forensic examination skills.")
H("677.d.1.B",4,"Earning a forensics certification helps a job seeker mainly by:","showing validated knowledge of investigation methods and tools",["replacing all experience","guaranteeing a promotion","avoiding background checks"],"Certifications signal verified skills.")
H("677.d.1.C",3,"Which government agency investigates federal cybercrimes and uses digital forensics?","the Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI)",["a city parks mural committee","a school cafeteria board","a local garden club"],"The FBI investigates federal cybercrime.")
H("677.d.1.C",4,"Which business is most likely to employ in-house digital forensics investigators?","a bank investigating fraud and data theft",["a car wash","a bakery with no computers","a roadside fruit stand"],"Financial firms face fraud and breaches.")
H("677.d.1.D",3,"Digital forensics specialists commonly investigate crimes such as:","fraud, identity theft and unauthorized network access",["jaywalking","littering","parking tickets"],"These crimes leave digital evidence.")
H("677.d.1.D",4,"Which crime would most likely require recovering deleted emails and file histories as evidence?","embezzlement carried out through accounting software",["a lost library book","a noisy neighbor","a missed bus"],"Financial crimes leave digital trails.")
H("677.d.2.A",3,"An effective plan to promote ethical online behavior in a school would include:","clear expectations, training and consequences for violations",["secret rules","no communication","rewarding rule breaking"],"Plans need expectations, education and accountability.")
H("677.d.2.A",4,"Which activity best advocates for legal behavior online among peers?","teaching classmates why copyright and privacy laws matter",["sharing pirated files","ignoring posts that break rules","hiding scam links"],"Education promotes lawful conduct.")
H("677.d.2.B",3,"Laws that govern when someone may access stored electronic communications are part of:","privacy and electronic communications law",["traffic law","maritime law","zoning law"],"These laws protect electronic communications.")
H("677.d.2.B",4,"The Stored Communications Act, part of ECPA, mainly limits:","unauthorized access to stored electronic communications",["driving speeds","building heights","food labels"],"It restricts access to stored messages.")
H("677.d.2.C",3,"Studying a historic digital forensics case helps students learn:","how investigators gathered and used evidence",["how to avoid all laws","which crimes are harmless","how to delete logs"],"Cases show real investigative methods.")
H("677.d.2.C",4,"Forensic investigations of major retail breaches showed that attacks can be traced back to:","their entry point, such as a compromised vendor account",["the CEO's lunch order","the store's paint color","the parking lot lights"],"Tracing identifies how attackers got in.")
H("677.d.2.D",3,"While examining a seized laptop, an investigator sees unrelated private family photos. The ethical action is to:","avoid sharing them and limit review to what the case requires",["post them online","show coworkers","keep copies"],"Investigators respect unrelated private data.")
H("677.d.2.D",4,"An investigator who finds privileged attorney-client emails on a device should:","stop and follow legal procedures for handling privileged material",["read them all","send them to the press","delete the device"],"Privileged material needs special handling.")
H("677.d.2.E",3,"When analyzing a computer incident case study, the first goal is usually to establish:","a timeline of what occurred",["the best desktop theme","the cheapest hardware","a new logo"],"Timelines organize events.")
H("677.d.2.E",4,"Comparing several incident case studies helps investigators:","recognize common attack patterns and mistakes",["avoid all future incidents guaranteed","ignore evidence","skip documentation"],"Patterns repeat across incidents.")
H("677.d.2.F",3,"Reconstructing an incident means:","using evidence to rebuild the sequence of events",["guessing without evidence","erasing the logs","blaming the newest employee"],"Reconstruction is evidence-based.")
H("677.d.2.F",4,"Which evidence combination best helps reconstruct who accessed a file and when?","access logs and file timestamps",["screen savers and wallpapers","keyboard brands","mouse pads"],"Logs and timestamps show who and when.")
H("677.d.2.G",3,"A legal right that protects original creative works such as software code is:","copyright",["zoning","probation","tariff"],"Copyright covers original works.")
H("677.d.2.G",4,"A secret formula or algorithm a company keeps confidential is protected as a:","trade secret",["public record","free sample","open license"],"Trade secrets are protected by secrecy.")
H("677.d.2.H",3,"Which method of gathering information is legal?","reading publicly posted company announcements",["guessing someone's password","installing spyware on a stranger's phone","breaking into a server"],"Public information is lawful to read.")
H("677.d.2.H",4,"An investigator needs a search warrant or consent before:","examining a person's private device",["reading a public website","viewing a press release","visiting a public library"],"Private devices are legally protected.")
H("677.d.2.I",3,"Which action is an ethical way to gather information for a case?","collecting only what is needed and documenting how it was obtained",["collecting everything possible secretly","falsifying notes","tricking people into sharing passwords"],"Ethical gathering is limited and documented.")
H("677.d.2.I",4,"Deceiving a witness by posing as someone else to obtain their data is generally considered:","unethical and possibly illegal",["a required procedure","a best practice","always allowed"],"Deception to get data violates ethics and law.")
H("677.d.2.J",3,"Growing public concern about data privacy has led to new:","laws that limit how personal data is collected",["laws banning all computers","rules requiring open passwords","taxes on keyboards"],"Privacy laws have expanded.")
H("677.d.2.J",4,"Which trend creates new legal questions for forensics investigators?","evidence stored in cloud services across countries",["typewriter repair","paper filing","handwritten letters only"],"Cross-border cloud data complicates jurisdiction.")
H("677.d.2.K",3,"Laws often lag behind technology because:","technology changes faster than legislation can be written",["lawmakers avoid computers by rule","courts forbid updates","technology never changes"],"Lawmaking is slower than innovation.")
H("677.d.2.K",4,"When new technology emerges, courts and legislators often:","update or reinterpret existing laws",["ignore the technology forever","ban all progress","delete old laws instantly"],"Law adapts to technology.")
H("677.d.3.A",3,"Using digital information responsibly includes:","protecting private data and following usage rules",["sharing it freely","altering evidence","ignoring policies"],"Responsible use protects privacy and follows rules.")
H("677.d.3.A",4,"A forensic analyst copies case data to a personal cloud account to work from home. This is:","a misuse of sensitive information",["required procedure","best practice","harmless convenience"],"Case data must stay in approved systems.")
H("677.d.3.B",3,"Using forensic software responsibly means using it only on:","systems you are authorized to examine",["any device you can reach","neighbors' networks","strangers' phones"],"Authorization defines allowed use.")
H("677.d.3.B",4,"Before using a powerful imaging tool on a device, you should confirm you have:","legal authorization and a documented purpose",["a faster computer","a new mouse","a bigger monitor"],"Authorization and purpose come first.")
H("677.d.3.C",3,"Which source is most reliable for learning how a forensic tool works?","the vendor's official documentation or a peer-reviewed study",["an anonymous forum rumor","a random video comment","an unsigned chain message"],"Official and reviewed sources are dependable.")
H("677.d.3.C",4,"To judge whether an online source is reliable, check its:","author credentials, evidence and date",["number of ads","background color","page loading animation"],"Credibility depends on expertise and evidence.")
H("677.d.3.D",3,"Informed consent means a person agrees after being told:","what will be examined and how it will be used",["nothing at all","only the time of day","a made-up reason"],"Consent requires understanding.")
H("677.d.3.D",4,"An employer wants to examine an employee's personal phone. Which step is most appropriate?","get the employee's informed consent or a legal order",["take it while they are away","guess the passcode","clone it secretly"],"Consent or legal authority is required.")
H("677.d.4.A",3,"Which is a common source of data in a digital forensic investigation?","hard drives and mobile phones",["lunch menus","parking permits","wall posters"],"Storage devices hold digital evidence.")
H("677.d.4.A",4,"Data stored on a suspect's online account would be collected from a:","cloud service provider",["paper shredder","desk drawer only","copy machine"],"Online data lives with the provider.")
H("677.d.4.B",3,"After analyzing collected data, an investigator should write a report that is:","clear, accurate and based on evidence",["vague and opinion-based","full of guesses","written to please the suspect"],"Reports must be factual.")
H("677.d.4.B",4,"A good forensic report separates:","facts found from the investigator's interpretations",["dates from times","files from folders","people from places"],"Readers must see what is fact and what is opinion.")
H("677.d.4.C",3,"Which practice helps keep collected evidence from being altered?","using a write blocker when copying a drive",["opening files and editing them","renaming every file","deleting temporary files"],"Write blockers prevent changes.")
H("677.d.4.C",4,"Encrypting stored evidence mainly protects its:","confidentiality",["color","weight","brand"],"Encryption keeps data private.")
H("677.d.4.D",3,"Metadata is best described as:","data about a file, such as its author and creation date",["the file's visible text only","a type of virus","a printer driver"],"Metadata describes other data.")
H("677.d.4.D",4,"A photo's metadata could reveal:","the date taken and the camera model",["the viewer's password","the next photo","the photographer's bank balance"],"EXIF data stores capture details.")
H("677.d.4.E",3,"Combining a phone's call log with network records is useful because it:","can confirm events by comparing independent sources",["replaces all evidence","hides contradictions","makes data unreadable"],"Corroboration strengthens findings.")
H("677.d.4.E",4,"Correlating logs from a server, a router and a laptop helps an investigator:","build a more complete timeline",["avoid documentation","lose context","delete duplicates"],"Multiple sources fill in gaps.")
H("677.d.5.A",3,"When comparing two forensic software applications, an investigator should consider:","supported file systems, accuracy and reporting features",["the theme color","the logo size","the splash screen music"],"Capability matters more than looks.")
H("677.d.5.A",4,"A forensic application that can read many file system types is more useful because it:","can examine more kinds of devices",["has a longer name","looks nicer","uses less paper"],"Broad support widens coverage.")
H("677.d.5.B",3,"Which application type would most likely hold evidence of a communication between two people?","an email client",["a calculator","a screen magnifier","a clock app"],"Email stores messages.")
H("677.d.5.B",4,"Peer-to-peer file sharing applications are of interest to investigators because they may be used to:","transfer illegal or stolen files",["print documents","adjust screen brightness","check spelling"],"File sharing can move illicit material.")
H("677.d.5.C",3,"A file ending in .jpeg is typically a(n):","image",["audio recording","program","spreadsheet"],"JPEG is an image format.")
H("677.d.5.C",4,"Why do investigators examine unknown .exe files carefully?","they can run code and may be malicious",["they are always images","they only hold audio","they can never change a system"],"Executables run programs.")
H("677.d.5.D",3,"An application log can show an investigator:","actions the program recorded, with times and users",["the software's price","the brand of the monitor","the user's favorite food"],"Logs record activity.")
H("677.d.5.D",4,"Database logs can help show whether someone:","queried or changed sensitive records",["changed the desktop theme","updated a font","adjusted screen volume"],"Database logs track data access.")
H("677.d.5.E",3,"A tool that creates an exact bit-for-bit copy of a drive is a:","disk imaging tool",["word processor","media player","photo editor"],"Imaging duplicates the entire drive.")
H("677.d.5.E",4,"Why do investigators work from a forensic image rather than the original drive?","to avoid changing the original evidence",["to make the case longer","to use more storage","to hide the original"],"The original must stay untouched.")
H("677.d.5.F",3,"Choosing a forensic tool based on whether it fits the task and works reliably shows attention to:","appropriateness and effectiveness",["brand loyalty only","package color","download wait time"],"Tools must fit the job and work well.")
H("677.d.5.F",4,"Two tools both recover deleted files, but one finishes in half the time. Which criterion favors it?","efficiency",["secrecy","decoration","humor"],"Efficiency measures time and resources.")
H("677.d.5.G",3,"A program's configuration file mainly stores:","settings that control how the application behaves",["the user's photos","the computer's serial number","the monitor resolution only"],"Config files hold settings.")
H("677.d.5.G",4,"Examining an application's support files and data folders may reveal:","user activity and stored information",["nothing about the user","only the app's icon","only the company logo"],"Apps leave traces in their folders.")
